WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.490
To keep up with today's computing demands,

2
00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:08.690
we need a cooling solution that goes
beyond air.

3
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:12.390
Direct liquid cooling or DLC delivers
coolant

4
00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.850
straight to the components that need it
most,

5
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.170
allowing systems to run at higher
densities

6
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:19.410
with greater efficiency.

7
00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:22.730
At the heart of DLC are cold plates,

8
00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:26.370
thin metal plates attached to CPUs and
GPUs.

9
00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.410
Coolant flows through engineered
microchannels

10
00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:32.210
inside the plate, absorbing heat directly

11
00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:36.090
at the source where it is generated.

12
00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.850
That heated fluid is then routed to a
coolant distribution

13
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.330
unit, or CDU.

14
00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:47.330
The CDU filters impurities, monitors
temperature and flow,

15
00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.550
and reconditions the liquid before sending
it back

16
00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:55.450
into circulation, ensuring reliability and
performance.

17
00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:59.730
This closed-loop design not only removes
heat more effectively

18
00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:03.410
than air, but also reduces fan noise,

19
00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.930
allows for tighter server density,

20
00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:10.130
and lowers the overall energy footprint of
the facility.

21
00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:13.170
Direct liquid cooling is a foundational
technology

22
00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:16.490
for the future of sustainable data
centers.

23
00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:19.730
A step that enables greater efficiency,
reliability,

24
00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:22.970
and scalability as workloads continue to
grow.
